WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.365
Good evening.

2
00:00:02.366 --> 00:00:06.098
Who are

3
00:00:06.099 --> 00:00:10.226
you? I'm a

4
00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:14.367
red fox. Red foxes

5
00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:18.838
are mammals. We look

6
00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:22.611
like dogs. Where do

7
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:25.431
you live? Red foxes

8
00:00:25.432 --> 00:00:30.862
live all over the world. We like

9
00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.063
forests. But we

10
00:00:34.064 --> 00:00:40.582
also live in cities and deserts. You

11
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:43.961
eat mice, right? Yes.

12
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:49.407
We eat other small animals too. We

13
00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:54.214
like birds and rabbits. Sometimes

14
00:00:54.215 --> 00:01:00.126
we eat fruit—and garbage. Your

15
00:01:00.127 --> 00:01:03.388
ears are big! Red

16
00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:07.453
foxes are good hunters. Our

17
00:01:07.454 --> 00:01:12.327
big ears help us hear prey. Who

18
00:01:12.328 --> 00:01:15.715
are your enemies? Coyotes

19
00:01:15.716 --> 00:01:19.730
and bears hunt us. People

20
00:01:19.731 --> 00:01:23.728
are our enemies too. They

21
00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:28.250
hunt us and build near our dens. Oh!

22
00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:31.967
Is that your den? Yes.

23
00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:36.663
We use dens for sleeping. Mother

24
00:01:36.664 --> 00:01:41.964
foxes keep their babies in dens.

25
00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:45.257
I like your bushy tail!

26
00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:49.409
We use our tails to cover our bodies.

27
00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:58.497
This keeps us warm at nap time.

28
00:01:58.498 --> 00:02:02.072
Shh. I hear a mouse.

29
00:02:02.073 --> 00:02:05.972
I'm going to hunt!

30
00:02:05.973 --> 00:02:11.180
So long, Red Fox!

